<h2>05.Corner Storage: Rescuing the Kitchen's Dead Zone</h2>
<p>Every <a href="/blogs/l-shape-kitchen-design/">L-shaped</a> and <a href="/blogs/u-shape-kitchen-design/">U-shaped kitchen</a> has at least one corner cabinet — and with a plain shelf inside, up to 60% of its volume becomes a black hole you reach into blind. Corner mechanisms exist to fix exactly this. The main options:</p>
<div class="table-wrap">
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Solution</th><th>How It Works</th><th>Access</th><th>Price Range</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Magic corner</td><td>Twin shelved frames: opening the door pulls the hidden set out and forward</td><td>★★★★★</td><td>₹12,000–30,000</td></tr>
    <tr><td>LeMans unit</td><td>Kidney-shaped trays swing out individually on an articulated arm</td><td>★★★★★</td><td>₹18,000–45,000</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Carousel / Lazy Susan</td><td>Rotating circular trays (270°/360°) spin contents to the door</td><td>★★★☆☆</td><td>₹6,000–15,000</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Half-moon / kidney basket</td><td>Semi-circular trays that swing out when the door opens</td><td>★★★☆☆</td><td>₹8,000–18,000</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Blind corner pull-out</td><td>Rail-mounted baskets slide out of the blind section</td><td>★★★★☆</td><td>₹10,000–25,000</td></tr>
