<h2>12.Matching Storage to Your Layout, Family &amp; Cooking Style</h2>
<h3>By kitchen layout</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Straight:</strong> no corners to solve — spend the savings on a full drawer bank and one tall pantry at the end.</li>
  <li><strong>Parallel:</strong> put cooking storage on the hob wall, washing/pantry on the other; two slim tall units bookending the runs work beautifully.</li>
  <li><strong>L-shaped:</strong> one corner to engineer (magic corner), tall units on the shorter arm. Full playbook in our <a href="/blogs/l-shape-kitchen-design/">L-shape kitchen guide</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>U-shaped:</strong> two corners — budget for two mechanisms or design one corner as an appliance garage. See our <a href="/blogs/u-shape-kitchen-design/">U-shape kitchen guide</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>Island / peninsula / G-shaped:</strong> islands add drawer real estate and can host the bin pull-out; peninsulas take the serving-zone storage; open-kitchen concepts push you toward handle-less, fully closed storage so the kitchen reads as furniture from the living room.</li>
</ul>
<h3>By family size &amp; lifestyle</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Singles &amp; couples:</strong> one drawer bank, compact pantry, appliance garage — prioritise counter clarity over volume.</li>
  <li><strong>Small families (3–4):</strong> the full essential set from this guide; add the vegetable basket unit and a proper plate-organizer drawer.</li>
  <li><strong>Large &amp; joint families:</strong> double the pantry (bulk grain storage), 70kg-rated deep drawers, two waste pull-outs, and a second cutlery station if two people cook simultaneously.</li>
  <li><strong>Daily heavy cooking:</strong> spice + oil pull-outs at the hob, tawa/kadhai deep drawer below it, and high-cycle-rated hardware — this kitchen opens every channel 40+ times a day.</li>
  <li><strong>Occasional cooks:</strong> spend on the appliance garage and display storage; skip specialty pull-outs you won't touch.</li>
  <li><strong>Baking enthusiasts:</strong> tray/baking-sheet dividers, a stand-mixer lift or garage, and one deep drawer dedicated to tins and moulds.</li>
</ul>
